  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and security. Key details include: \n\n- **Leadership & Team**: Led initially by Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole, with team expansions including members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing (e.g., Mike Chen, Lisa Ray). Omar Jensen leads the development phase.\n- **Timeline & Phases**: Kick-off occurred in June/July 2023. The project has moved from design to development. Onboarding for new members was scheduled for September 10th.\n- **Budget**: Phase one had a $500,000 allocation. The compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000. A specific training budget of $15,000 was approved for coding teams and project managers.\n- **Security & Compliance**: Security protocols were updated (MFA, encryption) effective January next year. Compliance efforts include training and third-party audits.\n- **Partnerships**: Discussions are underway with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology."
